        <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 14, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Complete and open (Oshtemo Twp). Construction ran through 2026.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; Shared-use trail, ~2 mi, 10-ft crushed limestone (not paved)&lt;br&gt;Former Fruit Belt rail corridor. Trailheads with paved parking at Flesher Field and 6th Street. Line geometry from the KATS October 2026 facilities layer.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.oshtemo.org/Departments/Parks-Recreation-Department/Fruit-Belt-Rail-Trail-Development"&gt;Oshtemo Twp – Fruit Belt Rail Trail Development&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.oshtemo.org/Departments/Media-Communications/Newsletter/Spring-2026-Newsletter"&gt;Oshtemo Twp – Spring 2026 Newsletter&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://services8.arcgis.com/iMB25Rg6ZW5ZL5YH/arcgis/rest/services/Existing_Facilities_October_2026/FeatureServer/0"&gt;KATS Existing Facilities October 2026 (ArcGIS layer, edited Oct 7, 2026)&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <styleUrl>#upd2026-sup</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>-85.71575,42.24501,0 -85.71073,42.24567,0 -85.70542,42.24638,0 -85.70127,42.24634,0 -85.69668,42.24631,0 -85.69503,42.24684,0 -85.69279,42.24819,0 -85.69118,42.24914,0 -85.68978,42.24997,0 -85.68941,42.25022,0 -85.68806,42.25112,0 -85.68635,42.25226,0 -85.68567,42.25271,0 -85.68415,42.25355,0 -85.68384,42.25372,0 -85.68199,42.25456,0 -85.67767,42.25651,0</coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>KL Ave path under US-131 (new 2026)</name>
        <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 14, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Open – KL Ave reopened June 11, 2026 after MDOT's US-131 bridge project.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; Shared-use path along KL Ave beneath the new US-131 bridges&lt;br&gt;MDOT has not published the path's exact limits or which side of KL Ave it is on, so it is shown as a point.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.michigan.gov/mdot/news-outreach/pressreleases/2026/06/11/kl-avenue-reopening-at-us-131-today-in-kalamazoo"&gt;MDOT – KL Avenue reopening at US-131 (June 11, 2026)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://wwmt.com/news/local/us-131-kl-avenue-bridge-project-kalamazoo-county-mdot-retaining-wall-shared-use-path-amtrak"&gt;WWMT – US-131 bridge replacement wraps up (June 11, 2026)&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <styleUrl>#upd2026-suppt</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-85.65610,42.27810,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Vicksburg Tr SUP – north end to Portage city limit (added Oct 2026)</name>
        <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 14, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Existing – shown as an existing shared-use path in the KATS facilities data; the club map's Vicksburg Tr line started about 0.5 mi farther south.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; Shared-use trail (Vicksburg Trail)&lt;br&gt;Fills the gap between the Austin Lake Trail's south end at the Portage city limit and the club map's Vicksburg Tr SUP. Drawn as a straight line along the old rail corridor (approximate).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://services8.arcgis.com/iMB25Rg6ZW5ZL5YH/arcgis/rest/services/Existing_Facilities_October_2026/FeatureServer/0"&gt;KATS Existing Facilities October 2026 (ArcGIS layer, edited Oct 7, 2026)&lt;/a&gt;</description>
        <styleUrl>#upd2026-sup</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>-85.53113,42.15742,0 -85.52875,42.15079,0</coordinates>
        </LineString>
      </Placemark>
