        <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 14, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Not open. County/Parks Foundation say east-end construction resumes in 2026; RCKC CIP lists $1.5M for this trailway in 2026. An agreement with Amtrak on the two rail crossings was reached in 2025.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; Kalamazoo River Valley Trail extension, ~4.5 mi&lt;br&gt;Alignment is the KATS planning line (approximate) – final route may differ. Starts at the east end of the existing KRVT (E6) segment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.kalamazoocountyroads.com/userfiles/kcrc/file/Projects/2026-2030%20CIP%20Approved%2012-16-2025.pdf"&gt;RCKC Primary Road CIP 2026–2030 (approved Dec 16, 2025)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.parksfoundationkalamazoo.com/parks-projects/"&gt;Parks Foundation of Kalamazoo County – Parks Projects&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.wmuk.org/wmuk-news/2025-05-30/kalamazoo-county-moves-to-close-a-major-gap-in-the-kalamazoo-river-valley-trail"&gt;WMUK – County moves to close KRVT gap (May 30, 2025)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://services8.arcgis.com/iMB25Rg6ZW5ZL5YH/arcgis/rest/services/Proposed_1_15_24/FeatureServer/0"&gt;KATS Proposed Facilities (ArcGIS layer, Jan 2024)&lt;/a&gt;</description>
