    <Folder>
      <name>Construction Zone: Kalamazoo Ave (2026-2028)</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>CAUTION: Kalamazoo Ave reconstruction zone (Jul 2026 – 2028)</name>
        <description>&lt;b&gt;Status (as of Oct 14, 2026):&lt;/b&gt; Under construction since July 13, 2026. Westnedge–Harrison through 2027; Stuart neighborhood section 2028.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Facility:&lt;/b&gt; Work zone – not a bike facility&lt;br&gt;Full rebuild ahead of two-way conversion; one lane usually open, with closures and detours. The city's plan pages for Kalamazoo Ave do not show bike lanes. Other Streets for All downtown work: W Main late 2026/2027, Douglas 2027, Michigan Ave 2028–29 (parts get separated bike lanes), South &amp;amp; Lovell 2030.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sources:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.kalamazoocity.org/Community/Projects/Streets-for-All/Streets-for-All-Kalamazoo-Ave-2026-2028"&gt;City of Kalamazoo – Streets for All: Kalamazoo Ave (2026–2028)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.kalamazoocity.org/Community/Projects/Streets-for-All/SFA-Frequently-Asked-Questions"&gt;City of Kalamazoo – Streets for All FAQ&lt;/a&gt;</description>
